{"agent":"w1-logsig","data":{"item":"B-af-log-signals","scope":"ddflow","severity":"medium","summary":"Only command gates (unit_tests) append gate.started (api/gates.py); rubber_duck/critic reviews record just an outcome event. Measured on this project's log: 128 gate.started, all unit_tests, zero for review gates, against ~600 review outcome events. flowsignals.reviewer_latency_ratio (started-to-outcome) is therefore None on every real log until review appends gate.started for the gate before it calls the reviewer. Fix: append gate.started in the review path (api/review) and add a test that review emits it.","title":"ddflow review never logs gate.started, so reviewer latency cannot be derived"},"id":"ef0bc18f40ebda5f1b8a07362","kind":"bug.found","lamport":12207,"schema":1,"subject":"B7ed5137d45","ts":"2026-10-03T10:30:14.695044Z"}
