{"agent":"w1-logsig","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The intent requires `independent_ready` to be the size of the conflict-aware independent set \"using the SAME selection as B-af-offer (shared helper, not a copy)\", and the failing-first test asserts it \"equals the count the offer would produce for the same state\". This implementation instead deep-copies the config, overwrites `schedule.max_parallel_tasks` and `worktree.max_parallel` with `10**6`, and returns `len(plan(state, wide, now=now).ready)`. Those two fields are precisely the knobs the offer uses to bound its selection, so the counts diverge whenever the caps bind: with `schedule.max_parallel_tasks = 4`, `worktree.max_parallel = 4`, 2 items already in flight and 7 mutually independent ready items, the offer can present only as many as its remaining slots allow, while this function returns 7 — the controller is fed a ready count the offer would never produce, and the stated equality test fails. Because the selection is re-derived here rather than obtained from the shared offer helper, the two computations can also drift silently whenever either side's selection logic changes.","digest":"8ad5cb1b8fda8666","location":"ddflow/core/flowsignals.py:113 `independent_ready`","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/flowsignals.py:113 `independent_ready`"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":16086,"diff_sha":"04f0748b7eb40e55248868e45bfc313578f57cc3098c9093fb146772f548ed92","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-af-log-signals","elapsed_s":667.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"37ef3dc279d63998","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/B-af-log-signals.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261003T103035-93b13923.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"d64e